Significant demand for a version of ALICE compatible withpre- Java 2 (formerly known as Java 1.2) prompted thedevelopment of "Bawt.java", an open source java programfor chat robot development that works with older versions ofJava, and AWT. Originally program B relied on Java 2 and Swing, but program Bawt needs only Java 1.1 and AWT.Swing is a newer GUI package that subsumes the earlier Java Abstract Windows Toolkit (AWT). At present class B merely extends class Bawt. Swing notsupported.
